            "review_text": "drzaikk\nKuala Lumpur, Malaysia8 contributions\n0\nMUSLIMS BEWARE! DUN STAY IN THIS HOTEL!\nJun 2012 • Family\nMy family of 6 stayed in this hotel for 3 nites. The first day was on 17th june followed by 19th june n 20th june 2012. No doubt the hotel is overall nice but we had a very bad experience there because the chef served pork in our fried rice. What was disgusting was we had specifically mentioned that we dun want any meat in our food. Infact just before eating we had asked again just to make sure there is no meat in our food. Being muslims we did not want to take any risks.However after nearly finishing our so-called seafood fried rice one of my family members was horrified to find a suspicious little piece of meat in the seafood fried rice n the chef later confirmed they had put a \"little\" bit of pork in our fried rice.\n\nLater we found another restaurant n hotel wch serves \"halal\" food. The food there was delicious n they made sure its halal for muslims too. Since its not advisable to advertise anything here , any muslims who wants to know the name of that restaurant may contact me directly n i will provide the contact numbers you need. I think its really disgusting for the staff n also chef of this hotel to hv ignored / not respect our wishes n even lied to us when we enquired whether there were any mest / pork in our food.\n\ni will definitely never step into this jotel again n i hope it also should be avoided by muslims if they choose to stay in hanoi.\n\nit definitely spoilt our family holiday.\nRead more\nValue\nRooms\nLocation\nCleanliness\nService\nSleep Quality\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten June 21, 2012\nHANOI BOUTIQUE HOTEL & SPA\nDear DrZaikk ! Warmest greetings from Hanoi Boutique Club . Firstly i'd like to appology for the inconvenience. Our new management had highly this mentioned case and make sure we will have the halal food/ no pork for the Muslim guest if there is an order at our restaurant. We are cooperating with Muslim Travel Agent and Vietnamese Muslim Comunity in Hanoi to get more understand about Islamic culture. We hope can welcome you and your family at Hanoi Boutique Hotel in the near future.\nBest regards,\nNguyen Thuy Duong\nRead more\nWritten February 19, 2014\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
